  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Militant Jihadism (2019), published by Leuven University Press, has no recorded citations yet, but it has been downloaded 3,330 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Militant Jihadism by Serafettin Pektas and Johan Leman was published by Leuven University Press in 2019. Conceptually, the work connects to Jihadism, Militant, Political science, Law and Politics.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records no citations for the book so far.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 3,330 times via OAPEN. It is recorded in 1 library collection. Its subject matter aligns with Gender equality among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 1 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
